    "result_text": "All done. The build succeeds and both tests pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key and duplicate detection as specified.\n\n**`Owner.java`** (`model/Owner.java`)\n- `getIdentityKey()` now returns the full lower-case hex **SHA-256** digest over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (previously the raw `telephone|email|householdId` string).\n- Added a standard **American Soundex** implementation (`public static String soundex`, plus `soundexCode`), correctly handling the h/w connector and vowel-separator rules, and a `sha256Hex` helper.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- `possibleDuplicateOf(...)` (the soft match) now triggers when **`soundex(lastName)` and postcode match but the whole identity key differs**, instead of the old \"same last name + postcode + different telephone\" rule. Since telephone is part of the key, same-lastName/same-postcode/different-telephone owners now fall through to a soft match (flagged, not 409) rather than a hard duplicate.\n- Updated the 409 check comment and `isIdentityKeyInUse` javadoc; the householdId no longer feeds duplicate detection (it's still computed for household size / membership-level capping).\n\n**`openapi.yml`**\n- Updated the `identityKey` description/example to the SHA-256 form (added a `^[0-9a-f]{64}$` pattern), and refreshed the `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` descriptions to reflect the Soundex-based soft match.\n\nThe email-domain blocklist still runs first (`validateEmailDomain` before the identity check), and deleted owners are still ignored in both the 409 and soft-match paths.",
